  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nOxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry in WW2: 6th Battalion\n£3.50\n\nOxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry in WW2: 6th Battalion quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\n \n\nOne of a a range of SOFO Museum's Battalion Booklets which each give an overview of the history of particular Oxford and Buckinghamshire LI battalions during the World Wars.\n\nResearched and written by James Pearson BA (Hons), previously an Archivist at the museum.\n\n19 pages.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nConflict & County\n£5.95 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre VI\n£5.00 Read more\nThe Royal Green Jackets Chronicle 1970\n£3.00 Add to cart\nMister Brownrigg’s Boys: Magdalen College School and the Great War\n£15.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
